# LIVE REGRESSION — a `&` sigil written INSIDE a closure body no longer
# silently drops the write; it now check-time REJECTS with
# `E_ReadWhileMutCaptured` on BOTH the projection row and the whole-bare-local
# row, matching the assignment spelling (`a.fd = 11`) which had this diagnostic
# from the start.
#
# INTERIM behaviour (Track U, Round XIII): reject. Under the ratified D7
# capture-syntax package the sigil belongs in a per-variable capture list —
# `(&count)(): ...` — at which point the boundary is spelled at the crossing
# and an in-body sigil path may relax. Until D7 lands, in-body sigil = reject
# so no user program relies on a silently-vanished write.
#
# ROOT (retired): `CapturedMutationCollector`
# (`src/semantic/safety/return_borrows.rs`) recognised THREE closure-body
# mutation forms — `Stmt::Assign`, `Stmt::CompoundAssign`, `&self` method
# receiver — with NO arm for `Ownership::MutableBorrow` call args. Track U
# added the fourth arm (Core #4: fix the class at the producer, not the
# instance) so both `Expr::Call` and `Expr::MethodCall` args classify the
# same as the receiver / assignment cases and flow through the existing
# `BorrowCaptureMode::Mutable` → `E_ReadWhileMutCaptured` machinery.
#
# BOUNDARY-MODEL rationale (why this is reference-grade): a boundary is where
# a value CROSSES FROM ONE SCOPE INTO ANOTHER, and the sigil is written AT the
# crossing. For a closure the crossing is at CAPTURE — Gorget infers the mode
# from the body until D7 lands — so an in-body sigil sits AFTER the crossing.
# Two spellings of one intent must not disagree; rejecting the vanished-write
# spelling keeps the language honest until the capture list arrives.
#
# ORACLE: ggdef cannot adjudicate — closures are outside the phase-0 subset.
# TWIN: `closure_amp_method_arg_body_reject.gg` covers the `Expr::MethodCall`
# arm; this file covers the `Expr::Call` arm.
#
# The seeds are COMPUTED, not literals, so const-folding cannot elide the store.

struct B:
    int fd

int seed():
    return 10

void bumpi(int &x):
    x = x + 1

void main():
    B b = B(seed())
    auto f1 = ():
        bumpi(&b.fd)
    f1()
    print(b.fd)

    int loc = seed()
    auto f2 = ():
        bumpi(&loc)
    f2()
    print(loc)
